  "inputs": {
    "html": "<html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charSet=\"UTF-8\" /><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=2496, height=1408\" /><meta data-composition-id=\"shot-still\" data-width=\"2496\" data-height=\"1408\" data-duration=\"1\" data-no-timeline=\"\" /><title>Shot still</title><link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Nunito:ital,wght@0,100;0,200;0,300;0,400;0,500;0,600;0,700;0,800;0,900;1,400;1,700&amp;display=block\" /><script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.15.0/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script><script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.15.0/dist/SplitText.min.js\"></script><script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.15.0/dist/DrawSVGPlugin.min.js\"></script><script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@tailwindcss/browser@4.3.3\"></script><style>\n@layer theme, base, components, utilities;\n@layer base { * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; } }\nhtml, body { width: 2496px; height: 1408px; overflow: hidden; background: #000; font-family: \"Nunito\", sans-serif; }\n#stage { position: absolute; top: 0px; left: 0px; width: 2496px; height: 1408px; overflow: hidden; }\n@layer components { .konte-clip { position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; visibility: hidden; object-fit: cover; } .konte-subtitle { inset: 0; width: auto; height: auto; display: flex; align-items: flex-end; justify-content: center; text-align: center; color: #fff; font-weight: 600; filter: drop-shadow(0 4px 4px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.15)); padding-bottom: 5%; font-size: 1.875vmax; } @media (orientation: portrait) { .konte-subtitle { padding-bottom: 15vh; font-size: 3.25vmax; } } }\n</style></head><body><div id=\"stage\"><style>#stage { background: #000000; }</style><div style=\"zoom:1.3\"><style>\n.ks{--font-mono:ui-monospace,\"SF Mono\",Menlo,Consolas,monospace;--bg-app:#0b0c0f;--bg-panel:#141519;--bg-input:#0f1014;--border:#23252d;--border-strong:#2e323c;--text-primary:#e7e9ee;--text-secondary:#9aa0ac;--text-muted:#686f7d;--accent:#6e62f5;--accent-hover:#8378ff;--accent-soft:rgba(110,98,245,.15);--green:#30c98e;--green-soft:rgba(48,201,142,.14);--red:#f25c5c;--orange:#f59e4b;--orange-soft:rgba(245,158,75,.14);\n  position:relative;width:1920px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--bg-app);color:var(--text-primary);font-size:14px;line-height:1.45;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;}\n.ks *{box-sizing:border-box;}\n.ks-app{max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 24px 48px;}\n.ks-header{position:relative;z-index:1;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:18px 0 14px;background:var(--bg-app);border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);}\n.ks-title{font-size:15px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.01em;}\n.ks-file{margin-left:auto;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:11px;color:var(--text-muted);}\n.ks-tabs{display:flex;gap:4px;}\n.ks-tab{font-size:13px;color:var(--text-secondary);border:1px solid transparent;border-radius:6px;padding:5px 12px;}\n.ks-tab.on{color:var(--text-primary);background:var(--accent-soft);border-color:var(--accent);}\n.ks-body{padding-top:20px;}\n.ks-intro{font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);max-width:62ch;margin-bottom:20px;}\n.ks-section{margin-bottom:28px;}\n.ks-h2{font-size:13px;font-weight:600;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;color:var(--text-secondary);margin-bottom:6px;}\n.ks-section-note{font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin-bottom:12px;max-width:62ch;}\n.ks-section-body{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px;background:var(--bg-panel);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;padding:16px;}\n.ks-field{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:5px;flex:1;}\n.ks-row{display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:flex-end;}\n.ks-label{font-size:12px;color:var(--text-secondary);}\n.ks-input{font-size:13px;color:var(--text-primary);background:var(--bg-input);border:1px solid var(--border-strong);border-radius:6px;padding:7px 10px;width:100%;min-height:32px;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;}\n.ks-input.focus{border-color:var(--accent);}\n.ks-input.ph{color:var(--text-muted);}\n.ks-note{display:block;font-size:11px;color:var(--text-muted);max-width:62ch;}\n.ks-note .ks-a{color:var(--accent-hover);text-decoration:underline;}\n.ks-code{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:10.5px;}\n.ks-toggle{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:9px;font-size:13px;}\n.ks-check{flex:none;margin-top:3px;width:13px;height:13px;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid var(--border-strong);background:var(--bg-input);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;}\n.ks-check.on{background:var(--accent);border-color:var(--accent);}\n.ks-link{align-self:flex-start;font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);text-decoration:underline;}\n.ks-cred{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;padding-bottom:14px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);}\n.ks-cred:last-child{padding-bottom:0;border-bottom:none;}\n.ks-cred-head{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;}\n.ks-cred-name{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:12px;}\n.ks-cred-label{font-size:12px;color:var(--text-secondary);}\n.ks-badge{font-size:10px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;border-radius:999px;padding:2px 8px;}\n.ks-badge.ok{color:var(--green);background:var(--green-soft);}\n.ks-badge.warn{color:var(--orange);background:var(--orange-soft);}\n.ks-badge.muted{color:var(--text-muted);background:rgba(255,255,255,.05);}\n.ks-footer{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:flex-end;gap:14px;padding-top:4px;}\n.ks-status{font-size:12px;}\n.ks-status.saved{color:var(--green);}\n.ks-status.error{color:var(--red);}\n.ks-primary{font-size:13px;font-weight:500;color:#fff;background:var(--accent);border-radius:6px;padding:8px 18px;}\n</style><div class=\"ks\" style=\"height:1080px\"><div class=\"ks-app\"><div class=\"ks-header\"><span class=\"ks-title\">konte settings</span><div class=\"ks-tabs\"><span class=\"ks-tab\">Config</span><span class=\"ks-tab on\">Credentials</span></div><span class=\"ks-file\">konte.credentials.json</span></div><div class=\"ks-body\" style=\"margin-top:0px\"><div class=\"ks-intro\">A stored value is never shown here, only whether it is set. konte loads these into the environment on every run, so a variable you export yourself always wins over the file.</div><div class=\"ks-section\"><div class=\"ks-h2\">Backends and model hosts</div><div class=\"ks-section-body\"><div class=\"ks-cred\"><div class=\"ks-cred-head\"><span class=\"ks-cred-name\">FAL_KEY</span><span class=\"ks-badge muted\">not set</span></div><span class=\"ks-cred-label\">fal.ai API key</span><div class=\"ks-field\"><span class=\"ks-label\">Value</span><div class=\"ks-input  \"></div><span class=\"ks-note\">Authenticates every fal.ai generation. <span class=\"ks-a\">https://fal.ai/dashboard/keys</span></span></div></div><div class=\"ks-cred\"><div class=\"ks-cred-head\"><span class=\"ks-cred-name\">COMFY_API_KEY</span><span class=\"ks-badge muted\">not set</span></div><span class=\"ks-cred-label\">Comfy API key</span><div class=\"ks-field\"><span class=\"ks-label\">Value</span><div class=\"ks-input focus \">••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••</div><span class=\"ks-note\">Authenticates Comfy API: Comfy Cloud (comfyapi:cloud) and your own deployments (comfyapi:&lt;name&gt;). Setting it is what lets a comfy adapter route to either. <span class=\"ks-a\">https://platform.comfy.org/profile/api-keys</span></span></div></div><div class=\"ks-cred\"><div class=\"ks-cred-head\"><span class=\"ks-cred-name\">HF_TOKEN</span><span class=\"ks-badge muted\">not set</span></div><span class=\"ks-cred-label\">HuggingFace access token</span><div class=\"ks-field\"><span class=\"ks-label\">Value</span><div class=\"ks-input  \"></div><span class=\"ks-note\">Only needed for gated or private repos. konte sends it as the bearer credential when it downloads a model from huggingface.co — keep the URL in the adapter plain. <span class=\"ks-a\">https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens</span></span></div></div><div class=\"ks-cred\"><div class=\"ks-cred-head\"><span class=\"ks-cred-name\">COMFYUI_TOKEN</span><span class=\"ks-badge muted\">not set</span></div><span class=\"ks-cred-label\">ComfyUI server credential</span><div class=\"ks-field\"><span class=\"ks-label\">Value</span><div class=\"ks-input  \"></div><span class=\"ks-note\">Only needed for a ComfyUI behind an auth front (a remote pod, a reverse proxy). Reference it from konte.config.json: &quot;comfy&quot;: { &quot;comfyui&quot;: { &quot;headers&quot;: { &quot;Authorization&quot;: &quot;Bearer ${COMFYUI_TOKEN}&quot; } } } <span class=\"ks-a\">https://docs.comfy.org/development/comfyui-server/comms_overview</span></span></div></div><div class=\"ks-cred\"><div class=\"ks-cred-head\"><span class=\"ks-cred-name\">CIVITAI_TOKEN</span><span class=\"ks-badge muted\">not set</span></div><span class=\"ks-cred-label\">Civitai API token</span><div class=\"ks-field\"><span class=\"ks-label\">Value</span><div class=\"ks-input  \"></div><span class=\"ks-note\">Used as the `?token=` query param, so an adapter's model URL writes it in: https://civitai.com/api/download/models/&lt;id&gt;?token=${CIVITAI_TOKEN} <span class=\"ks-a\">https://civitai.com/user/account</span></span></div></div></div></div><div class=\"ks-section\"><div class=\"ks-h2\">Add a key</div><div class=\"ks-section-note\">A custom adapter can name any variable in a model URL's ${VAR}.</div><div class=\"ks-section-body\"><div class=\"ks-field\"><span class=\"ks-label\">Name</span><div class=\"ks-input  ph\">MY_TOKEN</div></div><div class=\"ks-field\"><span class=\"ks-label\">Value</span><div class=\"ks-input  \"></div></div></div></div><div class=\"ks-footer\"><span class=\"ks-primary\">Save credentials</span></div></div></div></div></div></div></body></html>",
    "width": 2496,
    "height": 1408,
    "refs": []
  },
  "deterministic": true
